      "text": "Bogotá – Lake Guatavita – Zipaquirá"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "31289c572e7c679e8e949fdddd2edf448efaf8f324336b05e97057afe92f7064",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw9nvgw6-cx25ndvy",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set off at 08:00 with your English-speaking guide for a full-day excursion.\n\nFirst, head to Lake Guatavita. The lake is associated with the legend of El Dorado and the ceremony in which the Muisca people chose their chief. You’ll walk up to a viewpoint overlooking the lake. The programme includes a stop for lunch in the village of Guatavita.\n\nAfter lunch, continue to Zipaquirá, home to the famous Salt Cathedral carved into the rock salt. A dark tunnel leads to the interior chambers and the altar. The walls are about 75% salt. The site was once a working mine where local people extracted salt.\n\nReturn to Bogotá in the evening, check in and relax at the hotel."
    },
